# Remote styles #remote-styles

This example declares a stylesheet URL in front matter. The playground host fetches it, falls back to the local copy when needed, sanitizes it through the renderer, and applies it as an external stylesheet.

::section {.remote-hero}
## Loaded from a host resolver #loaded-from-host-resolver

The colored panel, badge, and grid below come from `remote-surface.nods`, not from an inline `::style` block.
::section

::section {.remote-grid}
:::note {.remote-card}
**Fetch**
The host loads a remote stylesheet URL.
:::note

:::note {.remote-card}
**Policy**
The renderer sanitizes CSS before output.
:::note

:::note {.remote-card}
**Fallback**
Local fallback keeps demos usable offline.
:::note
::section

Status: [[remote stylesheet active]].remote-badge.
